{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[A]Chickens a-crowing on Sourwood Mountain,
[E]Hey, ho, diddle-um [A]day,
[A]So many pretty girls I can't count 'em,
[E]Hey, ho, diddle-um [A]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[A]My true love's a blue-eyed daisy,
[E]Hey, ho, diddle-um [A]day,
[A]If I don't get her I'll go crazy,
[E]Hey, ho, diddle-um [A]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
[A]My true love lives up the river,
[E]Hey, ho, diddle-um [A]day,
[A]A few more jumps and I'll be with her,
[E]Hey, ho, diddle-um [A]day.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: A}
